# Which current detection architectures the graph engine could take, by op and by conv shape
# Host DESKTOP-CBL5NUA (Desktop 2, Ryzen 7 8700G), 2026-09-20, env resnet_env, ultralytics 8.4.142
# OFFLINE and STRUCTURAL. Each model is built from the YAML ultralytics ships, with RANDOM
# weights, and exported to ONNX at 640. No device, no accuracy, no latency: this says what
# would have to lower, never how well it would score.
#
# Command: python tools/arch_compat_audit.py yolo26n yolo26s yolo12n yolo11n yolov10n yolov8n
#
# YOLO26 is the newest family this toolchain ships. There is no YOLO27 in ultralytics 8.4.142
# (the families present are 26, 12, 11, v10, v9, v8, v6, v5, v3 and rt-detr), and whether one
# exists elsewhere was not established.
#
# What the engine accepts: 1x1 s1 p0, 3x3 s1 p1, 3x3 s2 p1, 5x5 s1 p2; MaxPool, Add, Resize x2,
# Concat and the Mul/Sigmoid epilogues; depthwise convolution only (group == Cin == Cout), and
# any dilation is refused (graph_ir.py:834-842 - it raises now, where an earlier revision read
# neither attribute and lowered a grouped conv as silently wrong arithmetic).
#
# The Div, Gather, Shape, Sub and one Softmax every row reports are the DFL and anchor decode
# tail, which the head cut removes before quantization - YOLOv8n lowers today carrying exactly
# that set. The row to read is "of which NOT decode": that is the attention a model would have
# to put on the host, and the bar is YOLO11n, which the engine already runs with one ONNX
# Runtime call per frame (0.51-0.53 ms).
=== yolo26n: 496 nodes, 102 convs
