# READING IT
#
# yolo26n is the most engine-compatible modern family here: ZERO unsupported conv shapes, and
# its only non-decode ops are 4 MatMul and 1 Softmax - one attention block's worth, the same
# shape of problem as yolo11n's C2PSA, which is already carved to the host and measured.
# Its 8 grouped convs must all be depthwise or lowering refuses; that was not checked here.
#
# yolo12n is a much larger lift: 8 convolutions of 7x7 (unsupported at any stride), 16 MatMul
# and 9 Softmax. Area attention runs through the whole backbone, not one block.
#
# NOT ESTABLISHED
#   - No model here was exported with real weights, head-cut, quantized, or lowered. This is a
#     node census, and a census can only rule a model OUT, never in.
#   - Whether yolo26n's grouped convolutions are depthwise.
#   - Whether the head cut for an NMS-free family (yolo26 is end-to-end) removes the same tail
#     it removes for yolov8n.
#   - Channel counts against the multiple-of-32 rule, and map sizes against the 20-pixel tile
#     floor, were not checked.
